Pale, hunched humanoids about three feet tall, bald and emaciated, with big floppy ears and white-blue skin. Their hands are stained with blood. They pick through what others leave behind: one was seen pulling clothing and junk out of a boat tied up in the sewers, sniffing each piece and tossing it behind it. They screech when a fight turns against them and break away.

They do not bleed. Opened through the chest, their flesh gives inward with no wound's worth of blood. They fight with clubs and long leaping charges.

In the sewers beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] they serve taller men in reddish-blued robe-armor, who carry staffs, cast spells and direct them. The men bleed like anyone, but one of them burst with a wave of dark energy when he was first wounded. Two of these men and two of their servants are dead; a third servant fled down a side passage.
